# SPA routing fallback (Cloudflare Pages format).
#
# Serve index.html (with a 200, not a 301) for any path that is not a real
# static file, so client-side routes like /properties/property-assessment
# survive a hard refresh or a shared deep link.
#
# Cloudflare Pages serves real static files (/assets, /data, /styles,
# /downloads, /manifest.json, ...) BEFORE applying this catch-all, so data and
# basemap loads are unaffected — only unmatched paths fall through to the SPA.
#
# Non-Pages hosts need their own equivalent — see README "Deploying the site"
# for the nginx try_files snippet.
/*  /index.html  200
